[501.19296, "o", "        <li>[2017-05-31] (<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/cafe0cc6d2cfa94aafc4f7193892fc4b0d07553e\">cafe0cc6</a>) Internal: Update \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K info for stable release</li>\r\n"]
[501.193561, "o", "    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.11.4\">\r\n    <p><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uyuni\" title=\"Wikipedia page for Uyuni, Bolivia\">Uyuni</a> is a small city that serves as a tourist gateway to the bare Uyuni salt flat. We wanted to use the name to transmit the idea that we are cleaning up (or laying down) the plans to move from all-timer \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 1 of Chamilo to \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 2. As such, this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K eliminates as many issues as we can possibly eliminate and contains as much clean-up as we can do before jumping to \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 2.0. Maybe this will not be the last of the 1.* releases, but it is certainly one of the latest steps before we eventually get there.</p>\r\n    There are 2 security fixes in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K, so we urge you to upgrade to this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K as soon as possible\r\n        <li>One <a href=\"https://support.chamilo.org/projects/chamilo-18/wiki/Security_issues#Issue-21-2016-07-15-Moderate-risk-User-Input-Sanitation\">fix for unsanitized user input</a>, present in Chamilo through the inclusion of an older \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K of the PHPMailer library</li>\r\n            that we offer our users. As such, in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K of Chamilo, the administrator *must* enable a configuration setting as follows\r\n"]
[501.19399, "o", "        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/b92fdadff66295d21456ed835e03ec156c8c578d\">b92fdadf</a>) Multi-URL: Change intra-\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K behaviour of configuration variable in different url.</li>"]
