[501.200429, "o", "\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/4184102685cf1314956206aacd9d0ce99476da74\">41841026</a>) Upgrade PHP \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K to 5.5 in composer.json, remove array_column package</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/c14fdf78b1b2a59d49520579c7ac1b4ed9c14926\">c14fdf78</a>) Add update-configuration to upgrade process from 1.10 to 1.11 to update the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K number</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/b0ff7b792373b9e3fab8aa1cd6ac6a1882253552\">b0ff7b79</a> - <a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/issues/1871\">GH#1871</a>) Fix phpoffice word dependency \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K (alternate configs in Composer to cover different PHP \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks)</li>\r\n"]
[501.201125, "o", "        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/ac8a66b240bcf92a9e83ec2f4c7e829747269a00\">ac8a66b2</a>) Update elfinder to latest \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K Important: requires composer update.</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/b6a700d38dff634a3728deb79851596d722655ef\">b6a700d3</a>) Add fixed \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K for fullcalendar.js</li>\r\n"]
[501.201645, "o", "        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/c0f31eae52637fdac661ccb614b18d495f924310\">c0f31eae</a> - <a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/issues/1413\">GH#1413</a>) Show the main url to upgrade \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K when using multi-url with the upgrader</li>"]
[501.201997, "o", "\r\n"]
[501.207762, "o", "        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/99d26f91dcd41cc994ce131c20186200d9b11d40\">99d26f91</a> - <a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/issues/1515\">GH#1515</a>) Fix \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K comparison on admin page</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/fe82c8a891130b05b9c446b0d1fd24c235e443b6\">fe82c8a8</a>) Plugins: Add IP filter option for the remote PPT con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K service</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/1e04af6720e7228853d3b0c71c1416255f02a6fb\">1e04af67</a>) Plugins: Add exception catching when calling remote ppt2lp con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/1c2933c343d7263d56463f94ba8f332cddc58349\">1c2933c3</a>) Migration: Add CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/be570c103d2d58581e4a2d4cbc7a25bf43ed3954\">be570c10</a>) Admin: Use \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K compare</li>\r\n    <p>A series of changes have been applied to the main/template/default/ folder in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K, so if you use your own template, make sure you update it to use the latest displays (otherwise some pages might fail and show TWIG-related error messages). Most notably:</p>\r\n        <li>A change has been made to include image2_chamilo in the ckeditor plugins in default/layout/header.js.tpl. If you have a custom \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K of this file, please search for the image2_chamilo text in the default TPL and make sure you apply the change, otherwise CKeditor might not display anymore.</li>\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.11.2\">\r\n    <p><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bari\" title=\"Wikipedia page for Bari, Italy\">Bari</a> is the capital city of the Metropolitan City of Bari and of the Apulia region, on the Adriatic Sea, in Italy. It is just a few hundred kilometers North of Lecce, the city which gave the name to our previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K. A bit more modern and a bit larger, it also hosts the infamous Basilica of Saint Nicholas, known as the \"Wonderworker\" for its miracles. Given 1.11.2 is just a perfecting release on top of 1.11.0, we felt the name of Bari was well suited for this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.</p>\r\n    <p>None in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.</p>\r\n    <p>None in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.</p>\r\n    <p>None in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.</p>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/d308e0bb5e5150d5bfbda652cd652e78fb15251f\">d308e0bb</a> - <a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/issues/1475\">GH#1475</a>) Add primary key as auto increment in c_student_publication_comment (fixes issue with migration from previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks)</li>\r\n        <p>None in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.</p>\r\n        <p>None in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.</p>\r\n        <p>None in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.</p>\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.11.0\">\r\n    <p>Chamilo 1.11.0 is a major release of the 1.11.x branch. It is meant as a transition between 1.10 and 2.0 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks.</p>\r\n    <p>None in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.</p>\r\n    <p>None in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.</p>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/9b5779acf8f8fc98c5fd219b333470e96773a7c6\">9b5779ac</a>) Add document size selector for teachers in Rapid PPT con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/48626533cae48e24183aefecf204fbf97919c4fd\">48626533</a> - <a href=\"https://support.chamilo.org/issues/8279\">#8279</a>) Add option to remove old crs tables from 1.8.x \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/dfa20396165a46600df0292fa9423434c127e2eb\">dfa20396</a>) Add md support for plugins. The readme file must be README.md in order to load the markdown con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/cha"]
[501.208958, "o", "milo/chamilo-lms/commit/4835cb52935e7169d8aef219a8563e0916f44d1c\">4835cb52</a>) Update ckeditor to \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 4.5.11</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/fa082097a00bfcab1f46658aa3c5011db09e1771\">fa082097</a>) Update \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K of required php-time-ago lib</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/3f8f859f71ea836449d4e225495d016f283d2634\">3f8f859f</a> - <a href=\"https://task.beeznest.com/issues/11588\">BT#11588</a>) Add changes to NULL values for DATETIME fields in tables migrated from previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/4e7fcba52e0543988049aa9d47b1a3c8e4efa0f3\">4e7fcba5</a> - <a href=\"https://support.chamilo.org/issues/8402\">#8402</a>) Re-establish Essence lib upstream repo in composer as a new \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K with the patch has been generated</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/222be4037e6b2beff689800facd9234c9e9fa062\">222be403</a>) Add 1.9.10.6 to \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks supported by migration</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/b122f061fce77310edf2a2c308ce15ce78e56acd\">b122f061</a> - <a href=\"https://support.chamilo.org/issues/8388\">#8388</a>) Decrease field lenght on \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K table</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/e1a3c19d8447cbc2a986ee3647d13a2651802f9c\">e1a3c19d</a>) Change \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K to support 5.4</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/9b5779acf8f8fc98c5fd219b333470e96773a7c6\">9b5779ac</a>) Add document size selector for teachers in Rapid PPT con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/3a3952389c7a1e70cd613513f698cec07292652f\">3a395238</a>) Use function to get all document con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K sizes (used in PPT con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K)</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/6c022643afbcfa94d40fc6606b2aba80a6a73aeb\">6c022643</a>) Add function to get all document con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K sizes (used in PPT con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K)</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/a8470af3d0fecd187e6c78de490284582743553e\">a8470af3</a>) Update \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K numbers in install scripts</li>\r\n"]
[501.20929, "o", "        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/e1a3c19d8447cbc2a986ee3647d13a2651802f9c\">e1a3c19d</a>) Change dependencies \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K to support 5.4</li>"]
[501.213291, "o", "\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/b21b87da7f384cc9d618cf51133b868493a8d789\">b21b87da</a> - <a href=\"https://support.chamilo.org/issues/8279\">#8279</a>) Update installation guide to add details about previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks tables</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/97580f2886bb3c0f243ece81e79424171f074b4b\">97580f28</a>) Fix installation add \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K table.</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/f70337a3fc82326fa3530b782641c76e3baa1906\">f70337a3</a>) Update \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K table (required to handle migrations via CLI)</li>\r\n"]
[501.214148, "o", "        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/884e589d72f9ddd156b617fa3ccd3fd53c713efd\">884e589d</a>) Update mpdf \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/e6d7edff139457b97fac9405f01a7bab59645f85\">e6d7edff</a> - <a href=\"https://support.chamilo.org/issues/8274\">#8274</a>) Fix course import from previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks #8274</li>\r\n"]
[501.214648, "o", "        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/0907a64acdf89143cb1aeec8fd3e76f54476e466\">0907a64a</a>) Update \"upgraded from \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks\"</li>"]
[501.214927, "o", "\r\n"]
[501.215333, "o", "        <li>Many changes have been made to the default template at main/template/default/, so if you have derived a custom template from it in previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks, you will have to work on the basis of the default again, most probably.</li>"]
[501.215607, "o", "\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.10.8\">\r\n        <li>Several security fixes were applied to this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K. Please update as soon as possible. You can find details of the vulnerability on <a href=\"https://support.chamilo.org/projects/chamilo-18/wiki/Security_issues\">Chamilo's security page</a></li>\r\n    <p>None in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.</p>\r\n"]
[501.216084, "o", "        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/f316e71b089c6383ab7372fda6f50167318771b4\">f316e71b</a> - <a href=\"https://support.chamilo.org/issues/8279\">#8279</a>) Update installation guide to add details about previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks tables</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/d5bbae840635f5652be59087b9f79e4bc3e9d170\">d5bbae84</a>) Add scayt plugin to fix issue with CKeditor and the spellchecker in previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K</li>\r\n"]
[501.217035, "o", "    <p>None in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.</p>\r\n    <p>None in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.</p>\r\n    <p>None in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.</p>\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.10.6\">\r\n    <p>None in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.</p>"]
[501.217257, "o", "\r\n    <p>None in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.</p>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/397c9dcfd1bccc648b78ba423b132ccacc5aae2a\">397c9dcf</a>) Update \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K to 1.10.6 in main/install/\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.php</li>\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.10.4\">\r\n    <p><a href=\"http://www.openstreetmap.org/node/1947201#map=14/51.3786/-2.3580\">Bath</a> is a small city of the South of England that inspires peace and stability, with its roman-age public baths and buildings. We feel like 1.10.4 is a very comforting \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K, fixing little issues people have found on previous 1.10.x \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks, and that the name suits it well.</p>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/e77104ae15496ad1619f678b8e62af8b0eb6a808\">e77104ae</a>) Fix default values in migration from previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/f283e196cbb036c768bd75b12fc27793990ecacc\">f283e196</a>) Fix default values in migration from previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/d7a97678ef81479cd0864711aad3ce0f12468311\">d7a97678</a>) TEXT Don't have default values in migration from previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks</li>"]
[501.217676, "o", "\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/06a87595066f2be340da82e3506d8e8e17ed8bdc\">06a87595</a> - <a href=\"https://task.beeznest.com/issues/10596\">BT#10596</a>) Fix issue with course info not available in Oogie documents con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K</li>"]
[501.218215, "o", "\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.10.2\">\r\n    <p>Chamilo 1.10.2 is a minor, bugfix \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K of the 1.10.x branch, with a few new features and  bugfixes on top of 1.10.0. Notably, this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K enables the migration from 1.9.x to 1.10.2 (many bugs were reported in the migration from 1.9.x to 1.10.0, which were fixed within the 2 months to this minor \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K).</p>\r\n"]
[501.218466, "o", "        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/a47f82e0a19379b4807bc7f830fbde98efbcafcb\">a47f82e0</a>) Fix problem with PHP 5.4 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K</li>\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/e656f5ac95d934d803f16dc147b9c00f57287b80\">e656f5ac</a> - <a href=\"https://support.chamilo.org/issues/8007\">#8007</a>) Update jplayer to latest \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K + fix player preview</li>"]
[501.218947, "o", "\r\n        <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/4c9a8d4a65ff1331d7a21714678969f07b0f957c\">4c9a8d4a</a>) Update FontAwesome \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K</li>\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.10.0\">\r\n<p>Chamilo 1.10.0 is a major \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K of the 1.10.x branch, with new features and bugfixes on top of 1.9.10. As a major \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K, it requires the use of the upgrade script in order to upgrade an existing Chamilo portal. See install instructions</p>\r\n    <li>\"Character set\" platform setting can't be modified. It is now fixed to UTF-8 (see #7652). This comes as a decision given the fact that other character encoding types were only there for backwards compatibility reasons, and that the last \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K with something else than UTF-8 was released more than 5 years ago.</li>"]
[501.219175, "o", "\r\n    <li>The hotspot question type is broken due to changes in the underlying Chamilo code. Given the fact this question type is developed in Flash and none of the developers at the time of release had Adobe CS available (proprietary technology that requires compilation) we have been unable to update the corresponding Flash code. Work is under way to provide the same feature using only HTML5, but it is likely to appear in a corrective \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K for 1.10.0. If you have an urgent need for this feature, please contact an official provider to get this sorted: providers@chamilo.org</li>\r\n    <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/4ff6568d67190413b78cc3f58043b0ecb1622d29\">4ff6568d</a> - <a href=\"https://task.beeznest.com/issues/7058\">BT#7058</a>) Add unoconv support to enable broader file formats exports and con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks (more in future \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks). This requires the installation of the UNO libraries on the server, so might not be available to all admins.</li>\r\n    <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/1a18a4cdd0bc2657f3d4c601b1c2a01a29593fb7\">1a18a4cd</a> - <a href=\"https://support.chamilo.org/issues/7485\">#7485</a>) Add con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K from single answer to multiple answer and viceversa</li>\r\n    <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/cb3f1a46287eb2557fd8767a1ff2dc07b7ee3a12\">cb3f1a46</a> - <a href=\"https://task.beeznest.com/issues/7721\">BT#7721</a>) Add branch tables (this will be further developed upon in future minor \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks and will enable multiple Chamilo instances to \"synchronize\")</li>\r\n    <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/ae13977673057b0e3e7175112bf26b399eb47ccd\">ae139776</a>) Remove chamilo_database_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K updates method - now using \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K table</li>"]
[501.21954, "o", "\r\n    <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/103e93771ef4d671b77649a0f28273acfab0fdc4\">103e9377</a>) Adding unoconv setting (multi-formats documents con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks)</li>\r\n    <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/6782df1b947d172e5a0990cf6664b3a804abd6dc\">6782df1b</a>) Add \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 1.10 migration.</li>"]
[501.219775, "o", "\r\n    <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/600335702b86bfd0f1172ab3ee51f6d90f9f6f67\">60033570</a>) Update jquery-ui \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 1.11.3</li>\r\n    <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/e1be9c9864bcf280aac058aa1127a95acd6e5d62\">e1be9c98</a>) Update fxp \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K requirement in README</li>"]
[501.222239, "o", "\r\n    <li>The hotspot question type is broken due to changes in the underlying Chamilo code. Given the fact this question type is developed in Flash and none of the developers at the time of release had Adobe CS available (proprietary technology that requires compilation) we have been unable to update the corresponding Flash code. Work is under way to provide the same feature using only HTML5, but it is likely to appear in a corrective \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K for 1.10.0. If you have an urgent need for this feature, please contact an official provider to get this sorted: providers@chamilo.org</li>\r\n<li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/49d6dfed77bac5c215895c106f067177d507904e\">49d6dfed</a>) Add small video con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K script. Might be useful for other things</li>\r\n    <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/503de2ab3b98702d59c50d90c6fdad8acfbb2f68\">503de2ab</a>) Remove chamilo_database_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K update. The filename has already the change number</li>"]
[501.222316, "o", "\r\n    <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/15d14d237da7997598612ce058f37908c65e2664\">15d14d23</a> - <a href=\"https://support.chamilo.org/issues/7672\">#7672</a>) Remove \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K number from footer and reformulate</li>\r\n    <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/695e77ab9ceeadf32f075e3de006fdb0d3b434d0\">695e77ab</a> - <a href=\"https://task.beeznest.com/issues/9885\">BT#9885</a>) Vendor - Add latest \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K of Select2</li>\r\n    <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/8c6427d4821ee405cd0acd83f483db05e158a16e\">8c6427d4</a>) Moving track_e_*.c_id filling queries to migrate-db to reduce execution by PHP. This updates chamilo_database_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K but it doesn't change the structure in any way.</li>\r\n    <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/cdf4d94607cc8028ec6008c5ba0ea46d9ea53e74\">cdf4d946</a>) Using stable \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K of php-ffmpeg</li>\r\n"]
[501.222506, "o", "    <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/3887d26ed8c66f657a6985e823ce5458989d3724\">3887d26e</a>) Update install documentation link to localized \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K for French, Spanish and Italian</li>"]
[501.222569, "o", "\r\n"]
[501.222694, "o", "    <li>Most of the CSS classes to most elements have been changed, making it practically impossible to maintain previous CSS styles with this new \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K (we're very sorry about that, but it was either this or sticking to non-mobile-friendly design)</li>"]
[501.222779, "o", "\r\n"]
[501.222864, "o", "  <li>The hotspot question type is broken due to changes in the underlying Chamilo code. Given the fact this question type is developed in Flash and none of the developers at the time of release had Adobe CS available (proprietary technology that requires compilation) we have been unable to update the corresponding Flash code. Work is under way to provide the same feature using only HTML5, but it is likely to appear in a corrective \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K for 1.10.0. If you have an urgent need for this feature, please contact an official provider to get this sorted: providers@chamilo.org</li>"]
[501.223069, "o", "\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.9.10.2\">\r\n  <p>Chamilo 1.9.10.2 is a patch (minor) \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K of the 1.9.x branch, with\r\n    vulnerabilities discovered in 1.9.10 and previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks (as such, you\r\n  offerings. We believe this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K of Chamilo, containing additional fixes on\r\n  top of an excellent 1.9.10 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K, has its fair share of common points with Sipán.</p>\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.9.10\">\r\n<p>Chamilo 1.9.10 is a new minor \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K of the 1.9.x branch, with many bugfixes and a few interesting new features (as such, you can just overwrite previous files to upgrade from 1.9.8, 1.9.8.1 or 1.9.8.2 to 1.9.10).</p>\r\n  \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K in memory of our cherished development team member César Perales, who\r\n  To this image, this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K marks a change of behaviour from the Chamilo team,\r\n  <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/25cd7ddc4928c76591dd983b05abf6a7cf929654\">25cd7ddc</a>) Use .gitattributes file to enable special Github features for \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks packaging</li>\r\n<li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/4c9a8d4a65ff1331d7a21714678969f07b0f957c\">4c9a8d4a</a>) Update FontAwesome \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K</li>\r\n"]
[501.223206, "o", "  <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/b83d51176db338399328b2b6d559bdee153c21e0\">b83d5117</a> - <a href=\"https://support.chamilo.org/issues/7325\">#7325</a>) Fix issue with the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K number not being extracted correctly from \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.chamilo.org/\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.php by an fread() on a HTTP socket</li>"]
[501.223339, "o", "\r\n"]
[501.223426, "o", "  <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/e344aae3f3bd08026632cd027b019303f0273ab0\">e344aae3</a> - <a href=\"https://task.beeznest.com/issues/6613\">BT#6613</a>) Deleting wav file if mp3 con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K succeeded</li>"]
[501.223484, "o", "\r\n"]
[501.223567, "o", "  <li>(<a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/b1d261db6f39591d839caece1de416027e9a438b\">b1d261db</a> - <a href=\"https://support.chamilo.org/issues/7320\">#7320</a>) Update Twig to \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K v1.16.0 + move to vendor folder</li>"]
[501.224101, "o", "\r\n  <li>No major style changes in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K, but a lot of visual improvements</li>\r\n  <li>No removal worth mentioning in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K</li>\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.9.8.2\">\r\n        <p>Chamilo 1.9.8.2 is a very little patch \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K with one bugfix regarding the learning paths tool. Considering the fact that 1.9.8 is planned for the long term, we'd hate to have such a minor patch left on the side for a year or so. This will be packaged and promoted as 1.9.8, but the folder inside the 1.9.8 will be called 1.9.8.2, with a change to this changelog file and a one-line change to main/newscorm/learnpathItem.class.php (as such, you can update just this file to upgrade from 1.9.8.1 to 1.9.8.2. See <a href=\"https://github.com/chamilo/chamilo-lms/commit/642a80e9e838f98f25135fbb64795e4f3df86260\">the code change</a> for details.</p>\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.9.8.1\">\r\n        <p>Chamilo 1.9.8.1 is a patch \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K with one security patch on top of 1.9.8 (in the included library for FCKeditor). Please check <a href=\"https://support.chamilo.org/projects/chamilo-18/wiki/Security_issues\">our security issues page</a> for more information.</p>\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.9.8.0\">\r\n<p>Chamilo 1.9.8 is a minor stable \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K with a series of improvements on top of 1.9.6.<br />\r\nThis \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K is the first Chamilo \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K to drop support for Internet Explorer\r\nleast \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 10, which respects a little bit more than half of the W3C\r\n<p><a href=\"http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thon-Samson\">Thon</a> is a small city in the Belgian region of Wallonia, several times classified as the most beautiful village of the South region of Belgium. It is a quite, beautiful place without anything out of the ordinary but made of beautiful, hundred years old homes built from famous Wallonia blue stone and crossed by the Samson river. Its stability and it's position just next to the large cliffs surrounding the Meuse are symbolically close to Chamilo 1.9.8, highly stable but a few steps away for the huge jump to the next major \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.</p>\r\n    <li>(#6216) Make check_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K() AJAX-based</li>\r\n    <li>(#6877) Information missing in Assignment page comparing to previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K</li>\r\n    <li>(03b46d3) Update jQGrid \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K to 4.5.2</li>\r\n    <li>(a5f40a2 - BT#7644) Change of con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K number from bytes to MB</li>\r\nStylesheets have been considerably changed in \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 1.9.8, which might require a little update on your side if you have a custom stylesheet. We're sorry about it, but it was really necessary to improve the adaptability of the interface for mobile devices (which we are sure you will appreciate). If you only changed the logo, we recommend you make a copy of an existing Chamilo style (main/css/chamilo*) again, rename it and simply replace the logo then upload the new style. If you have more complex styles, you might want to ask for the assistance of your web designer at the moment you update Chamilo to this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.9.6.1\">\r\n<p>Chamilo 1.9.6.1 is a patch \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K with security patches on top of 1.9.6. Please check <a href=\"https://support.chamilo.org/projects/chamilo-18/wiki/Security_issues\">our security issues page</a> for more information.</p>\r\n<div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.9.6.0\">\r\n<p>Chamilo 1.9.6 is a minor stable \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K with security patches and a series of improvements on top of 1.9.4.</p>\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.9.4\">\r\n<p>Chamilo 1.9.4 is a minor stable \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K with a series of improvements on top of 1.9.2.</p>\r\n  <li>Internal/Development: First running \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K of continuous integration build system at http://testing.chamilo.org/ usin"]
[501.224171, "o", "g PHPUnit</li>\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.9.2\">"]
[501.22576, "o", "\r\n<p>Chamilo 1.9.2 is a minor stable \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K with a series of improvements on top of 1.9.0.</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanga_Roa\">Hanga Roa</a> is the capital city of Rapa Nui, the Easter Island. The entire Rapa Nui culture is filled with mystery and assumptions about where and how the first Rapa Nui people came to be on the island, but it is accepted by many that the main strain came from Polynesia a long time ago. The population there is around 3,300 but warmly welcomes tons of tourists every year, a bit in the image of the small team of Chamilo now serving more than 1.4M users worldwide, with a welcoming 1.9.2 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K that will help you get more time to yourself...</p>\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.9.0\">\r\n<p>Chamilo 1.9.0 is a major stable \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K with loads of added features.</p>\r\nThis \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K of Chamilo includes a few new features.\r\n  <li>Documents: Updated SVG-edit tool to latest \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K and included external SVG galleries (#4399, #4408)</li>\r\n  <li>Admin: update_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K variable not used (#4711)</li>\r\n  <li>Wiki: wiki all pages - each page is not the last \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K (#3848)</li>\r\n    <li>Fullcalendar js library \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 1.5.2</li>\r\n<div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.8.8.6\">\r\n<p>Chamilo 1.8.8.6 is a minor security fix, stable \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K for \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 1.8.8.4. If you are using Chamilo 1.8.8.4, we highly recommend you upgrade to this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K, either by following the usual upgrade procedure, or by applying a very small patch, as explained on <a href=\"http://support.chamilo.org/projects/chamilo-18/wiki/Security_issues\">our security issues listing page</a>. The security fixes are all considered \"moderate\". This means you could loose data (specifically dropbox tool data in this case) and your users might get tricked into providing credentials to potential hackers, but the integrity of your server will not be in direct danger. 1.8.8.6 was developed in a separate branch, but fixes were applied to the 1.9 branch, which means 1.9 can be considered as the follower of 1.8.8.6 as much as of 1.8.8.4. If you have 1.8.8.4, migrating to 1.9 will effectively remove the need for migrating to the intermediary step of 1.8.8.6</p>\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.8.8.4\">\r\n<p>Chamilo 1.8.8.4 is a minor corrective stable \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K for \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 1.8.8.2 with a bunch of new minor features added.</p>\r\nThis \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K of Chamilo only includes a few minor new features:\r\n  <li>Added quick browsing of directories' documents - requires manual activation for now: in user_portal.php, find $load_dirs and set to $load_dirs = true;. Will be setable through admin page in next \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K (changeset 7f84869233c2)</li>\r\n    <li>Jquery updated to \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 1.6.2</li>"]
[501.225918, "o", "\r\n    <li>Jquery-ui updated from \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 1.8.7 to 1.8.16</li>\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.8.8.2\">\r\n<p>Chamilo 1.8.8.2 is a minor corrective stable \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K for \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 1.8.8 to enable easier install on shared hosting.</p>\r\n  <li>If you used split users directories before v1.8.8 in combination with the \"My files\" feature (if it existed at all at that point), you will probably have a problem now, as the code in the previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K was wrong and was saving the personal portfolio file in another directory than the user's. Sorry about that. If you need professional assistance, see the http://www.chamilo.org/ website under support -> professional support for official providers who could help you. And don't forget to keep a backup. If you don't understand a thing about what I'm talking about, you are probable not concerned by this bug, so don't worry too much.</li>"]
[501.226081, "o", "\r\n"]
[501.226202, "o", "    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.8.8\">"]
[501.22631, "o", "\r\n"]
[501.2897, "o", "<p>Chamilo 1.8.8 is a major stable \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K. Although it doesn't come with a strong redesign, it provides a large number of small improvements to the teacher's toolset and the user's using pleasure. Audio recording, schema drawing, certification generating, better administration features, plugin for videoconference with BigBlueButton and e-commerce with PrestaShop are only a few of the improvements that you will find in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K.</p>\r\n   <li>Access details: Now we can filter the access details of a user by date 3258# First \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K developved by Jorge Frisancho Jibaja - USIL</li>\r\n  <li>Fixed charset con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K problems in previous migrations to Chamilo 1.8.7.1 (#1765)</li>\r\n  <li>Fixed bad con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K of course title after upgrade (#3231)</li>\r\n  <li>If you used split users directories before v1.8.8 in combination with the \"My files\" feature (if it existed at all at that point), you will probably have a problem now, as the code in the previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K was wrong and was saving the personal portfolio file in another directory than the user's. Sorry about that. If you need professional assistance, see the http://www.chamilo.org/ website under support -> professional support for official providers who could help you. And don't forget to keep a backup. If you don't understand a thing about what I'm talking about, you are probable not concerned by this bug, so don't worry too much.</li>\r\n<div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.8.7.1\">\r\n  <li>ASCIIMathML.js: The script for showing mathematical formulas has been upgraded from \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 2.0.2 to \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 2.1. Additional changes have been made in the online editor's plugin asciimath (Feature #541)</li>\r\n  <li>The mPDF library (which is used for PDF-files generation) has been upgraded from \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 4.2 to \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 4.6 (Feature #1656)</li>\r\n\r100 3147k  100 3147k    0     0  18.1M      0 --:--:-- --:--:-- --:--:-- 18.5M\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.8.7\">\r\n<p>Chamilo 1.8.7 is a major&nbsp;release including a lot of new features, mostly focused on social network, the handling of sessions (which will help many educational institutions, public or private, to manage their contents in a more flexible way) and visual style, and a few important bugfixes. It lays the first stable stone in the Chamilo software project. This \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K is the first one to <b>highly recommend PHP 5.2</b> or superior, and <b>require PHP 5.1</b> or higher.<br />Also, this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K of Chamilo will automatically convert all your data to UTF-8, which will make it more difficult to migrate from Dokeos \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks higher than 1.8.6.1</p>\r\n    <li>For upgraded systems: The upgrade procedure automatically changes the character set to UTF-8. During upgrade database tables are converted to UTF-8 and the corresponding changes to text fields are applied. Con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K to UTF-8 of HTML documents stored in the file system is not performed, this is not mandatory.</li>\r\n    <li><em>Note about integration with external systems</em>: Keep in mind that since \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 1.8.7, pieces of text kept in the database are UTF-8 encoded. If an external system accesses database records directly, some corrections to contents of the external database might be necessary.</li>\r\n  <li>Upgraded PclZip library to \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 2.8.2 (Feature #553)</li>\r\n  <li>Upgraded PHPMailer library to \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 5.1 (Feature #272)</li>\r\n  <li>Updating license \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K to GNU/GPL v3</li>\r\n  <li>Core API: Support has been implemented for json_encode() function for PHP \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K &#60; 5.2. The correspondent bug-report \"Hide and show not working\" and testing have been done by Hubert Borderiou <a href=\"http://support.chamilo.org/issues/761\" target=\"_blank\">http://support.chamilo.org/issues/761</a></li>\r\n  <li>Timezone functionality is "]
[501.289827, "o", "not available in the most recent \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks of PHP available for CentOS/RHEL ( 5.1.6-23.2.el5_3 ) (see http://www.php.net/manual/en/function.timezone-identifiers-list.php). Chamilo now requires PHP 5.1 or superior and <b>highly</b> recommends PHP 5.2.</li>\r\n  <li>HTMLPurifier updated to \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 4.1.0</li>\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.8.6.2\">\r\n  <li>Added posibility to establish a max number of \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks for each wiki page</li>\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.8.6.1\">\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.8.6\">\r\n  <li>The PclZip library has been upgraded to \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K 2.6. Additionally, a known  bug has been fixed - improper processing of the option PCLZIP_OPT_REMOVE_PATH on Windows (FS#3243)</li>\r\n  <li>Removed possibility to create sub-directories in the dropbox tool - wasn't working anyway for various \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks (FS#3434)</li>\r\n  <li>Fixed a bug in migration for several \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks at once whereby new course tools were repeated several times (SVN#17935)</li>\r\n  <li>Fixed bug with user image not showing in upgrade from previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks</li>\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.8.5\">\r\n                latest stable \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.8.4\">\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.8.0\">\r\n      <li> Ms-PowerPoint® to Learning Path con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K</li>\r\n      <li>Documents tool: PowerPoint and Word into HTML file type  con\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K</li>\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.6.5\">\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.6.4\">\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.6.3\">\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.6.2\">\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.6.1\">\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.6.0\">\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.5.5\">\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.4.2\">\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.4.1\">\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.4.0\">\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.3.1\">\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.3.0\">\r\n        <li>WEB INSTALL. New functions allowing to upgrade from 1.2 and 1.1 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks\r\n    <div class=\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K\" aria-label=\"1.2.0\">\r\n            size calculation works with PHP 4.1+ (no problem with previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks).</li>\r\n        Each \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K is shortly described, with:\r\n        <li>a \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K number using <a href=\"http://semver.org/\">Semantic Versioning</a></li>\r\n        <li>a \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K name, which is the name of a town or village visited at least once by one of our development team members, preferably with a link to the place in OpenStreetmap or on Wikipedia</li>\r\n        <li>an optional, short history explaining the relationship between the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K and the place</li>\r\n        Inside each \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K block, different sections are laid out to ease the reading of the changelog:\r\n        <li>Security fixes: indicate if any known vulnerability was fixed in this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K. This section is very important as each \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K with a vulnerability fix indicates that you should *really* upgrade to that \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K if you value your Chamilo portal's security and the data of your users</li>\r\n        <li>Possibly breaking changes: indicate if any change we made in Chamilo is non-backwards compatible, meaning something will break if you upgrade to this \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K from a previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K (rather than installing it fresh) without taking some special action</li>\r\n        <li>Notable new Features: lists (in two different subsections) the features that are most like"]
[501.289887, "o", "ly to be noted by normal Chamilo users when changing \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks, or that are most likely to be directly useful to them.</li>\r\n        <li>Improvements (minor features) and debug: an almost unfiltered list of fixes and improvements that have been made between the previous \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K and this new one. We remove all \"Minor\" commits, all unit testing commits, all minor visual fixes (icons and stuff) and as many duplicate topics as we can, with the goal to give you a series of links to the changes from which you can find all the related changes by yourself from their Git history if you need them.</li>\r\n        <li>Web services: if you integrate Chamilo with some other tool through the use of web services, make sure you check this section to know what's new and what has changed, as you might need to change your integration to make it work with this new \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K. Of course, we try to make the less changes possible and prefer creating new methods than modifying old ones, but sometimes security issues might force us to do so.</li>\r\n        <li>Removals: when a tool or stylesheet is not maintained anymore, or when we replaced some library with another, we will remove deprecated files. This is a list of such files that might have been removed or simply marked for deprecation or removal in later \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks.</li>\r\n        Every change comes with a link to the change in our \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[Ks tracking system, a link to the reported issue or task (if any) and a description of the change's purpose.\r\n        We use a short terminology to try and group all changes applying to the same tool. We use the singular \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kversion\u001b[m\u001b[K. The names we use for these tools are:\r\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            \r\r\u001b]0;david@kali: ~\u0007\r\n"]
[501.295759, "o", "\r\u001b[0m\u001b[27m\u001b[24m\u001b[J\u001b[32m┌──(\u001b[1m\u001b[32m\u001b[34mdavid㉿kali\u001b[0m\u001b[34m\u001b[32m)-[\u001b[1m\u001b[32m\u001b[39m~\u001b[0m\u001b[32m]"]
